From: mumu-patch
Subject: [PATCH] Task.java: drop the PersistedTaskSnapshotData reference for SDK 35

The launcher is installed on Android 15 (SDK 35), where
android.app.ActivityManager$RecentTaskInfo$PersistedTaskSnapshotData does not
exist -- it is newer than this platform.  Two things in this file name it:

  * the declared type of Task.lastSnapshotData;
  * RecentTaskInfo.lastSnapshotData, a *platform* field of that type.

Both make ART's class verifier reject the whole class:

  java.lang.VerifyError: Verifier rejected class
      com.android.systemui.shared.recents.model.Task:
      void ...Task.<init>(Task) failed to verify:
      [0x16] 'this' argument 'Reference java.lang.Object' not instance of
      'Unresolved Reference:
       android.app.ActivityManager$RecentTaskInfo$PersistedTaskSnapshotData'

and because Task is built while loading the task list, the Recents screen
crashes with it.

Rewriting the *field declarations* to java.lang.Object is not enough, and
neither is an SDK_INT guard: the verifier resolves every type a method
mentions, so the reference has to be removed from the code.  This replaces it
with a local stand-in of the same shape.  Nothing populates it, so
getVisibleThumbnailRatio() reports 0f, which is the documented "snapshot data
is not available" answer -- the data was never available on this platform
anyway.

Apply with:

    git clone --depth 1 --branch v15.0.0-beta3.0 \
        https://github.com/LawnchairLauncher/lawnchair.git
    cd lawnchair
    git apply /path/to/lawnchair-sdk35-recents.patch

diff --git a/systemUI/shared/src/com/android/systemui/shared/recents/model/Task.java b/systemUI/shared/src/com/android/systemui/shared/recents/model/Task.java
index f06e333..fe6fba4 100644
--- a/systemUI/shared/src/com/android/systemui/shared/recents/model/Task.java
+++ b/systemUI/shared/src/com/android/systemui/shared/recents/model/Task.java
@@ -242,9 +242,35 @@ public class Task {
 
     public Rect appBounds;
 
-    // Last snapshot data, only used for recent tasks
-    public ActivityManager.RecentTaskInfo.PersistedTaskSnapshotData lastSnapshotData =
-            new ActivityManager.RecentTaskInfo.PersistedTaskSnapshotData();
+    // Last snapshot data, only used for recent tasks.
+    //
+    // This was ActivityManager.RecentTaskInfo.PersistedTaskSnapshotData, a type
+    // that does not exist on Android 15 (SDK 35), which is what this launcher is
+    // installed on.  The class verifier resolves every type a method mentions,
+    // so an SDK_INT guard is not enough -- the reference itself has to go, or
+    // the whole Task class is rejected with
+    //   VerifyError: ... not instance of 'Unresolved Reference:
+    //   android.app.ActivityManager$RecentTaskInfo$PersistedTaskSnapshotData'
+    // and the Recents screen crashes.
+    //
+    // The stand-in keeps the shape the rest of the file uses.  Nothing ever
+    // fills it in, so getVisibleThumbnailRatio() returns 0f, which is the
+    // documented answer for "snapshot data is not available".
+    public SnapshotData lastSnapshotData = new SnapshotData();
+
+    /** Stand-in for the platform snapshot type, which this SDK does not have. */
+    public static final class SnapshotData {
+        public Point taskSize;
+        public Rect contentInsets;
+
+        public void set(SnapshotData other) {
+            if (other == null) {
+                return;
+            }
+            this.taskSize = other.taskSize;
+            this.contentInsets = other.contentInsets;
+        }
+    }
 
     public Task() {
         // Do nothing
@@ -307,7 +333,9 @@ public class Task {
     }
 
     public void setLastSnapshotData(ActivityManager.RecentTaskInfo rawTask) {
-        lastSnapshotData.set(rawTask.lastSnapshotData);
+        // RecentTaskInfo carries no snapshot data on this platform -- the field
+        // this used to read is part of the same missing type -- so there is
+        // nothing to copy.  Kept because callers exist.
     }
 
     public TaskKey getKey() {
